/// Plug — composable request/response middleware for HTTP handlers.
///
/// A Plug wraps the *next* step of a handler pipeline. It can inspect or
/// transform the request before passing it on, short-circuit by returning
/// a response of its own without calling `next` at all, or post-process
/// whatever `next` returns (add headers, log timing, catch errors) before
/// returning it upward. This is the same "onion" composition Rack, Plug,
/// and Express-style middleware use, expressed as a plain protocol so any
/// Value can implement it.
///
/// A Plug runs wherever the handler it's chained into runs. For a block or
/// `HTTPRouter` route handler, that's outside the owning actor's process
/// (see `HTTPRouter` docs) — `self.field` reads inside a Plug only ever
/// see whatever was captured when the chain was built. A Plug that needs
/// live, mutable actor state should be backed by an actor implementing
/// `HTTPHandler>>handle:` instead, not by `PlugChain`.
///
/// ## Writing a Plug
/// ```beamtalk
/// Value subclass: RequestLogger
///   call: request :: HTTPRequest next: next :: Block(HTTPRequest, HTTPResponse) -> HTTPResponse =>
///     response := next value: request
///     Logger info: request method ++ " " ++ request path ++ " -> " ++ response status printString
///     response
/// ```
///
/// ## Example
/// ```beamtalk
/// pipeline := PlugChain
///   chain: #(RequestLogger new)
///   handler: [:req | HTTPResponse new: #{ #status => 200, #body => "ok" }]
/// srv := HTTPServer start: 8080 handler: pipeline
/// ```
///
/// @see PlugChain (composes a list of Plugs into a single handler block)
/// @see HTTPHandler (the actor-pid handler style, for live actor state)
/// @see RequestLogger (a ready-made request-logging Plug)
Protocol define: Plug
  /// Handle `request`. Call `next value: request` (or a transformed
  /// request) to continue the pipeline and receive the downstream
  /// `HTTPResponse`, or return a response directly without calling `next`
  /// to short-circuit the rest of the chain.
  call: request :: HTTPRequest next: next :: Block(HTTPRequest, HTTPResponse) -> HTTPResponse
